.TH MEWL 1 "March 5, 2003"
.SH NAME
mewl - Message scanner for Mew 4 or later
.\"
.SH SYNOPSIS
mewl
.RI [ options ]
.RI [ folder
.RI [ range ]]
.\"
.SH DESCRIPTION
The
.B mewl
utility extracts necessary fields from messages stored in folders.
This command is necessary for Mew to implement the asynchronous feature.
.PP
The options are as follows:
.TP 8
.B \-a
Print all necessary fields when picking.
.TP 8
.BI \-b " dir"
Set the Mail home to
.IR dir .
.TP 8
.BI \-c " bodylen"
Set the max body length to be extracted to
.IR bodylen .
.TP 8
.BI \-d " field"
Set the field to be extracted to
.IR field .
.TP 8
.BI \-e " command"
Specify an external
.I command
to fetch mailbox.
.TP 8
.BI \-m " options"
Specify 
.I options
for
.IR command .
.TP 8
.BI \-f " fields"
Specify 
.I fields
to display.
.TP 8
.B \-h
Display this help message.
.TP 8
.BI \-i " file"
Set the input stream to
.IR file .
.TP 8
.BI \-l " length"
Set the max field length to be extracted to
.IR length .
The default value is 3. 0 means no limit.
.TP 8
.B \-n
Don't use fstat().
.TP 8
.BI \-p " pattern"
Specify the pick
.IR pattern .
.TP 8
.BI \-s " src"
Set message source to
.I src
: '+folder range'.
.TP 8
.B \-w
Wait for stdio input to synchronize.
.TP 8
.B \-v
Display the version.
.TP 8
.BI \-x " suffix"
Use this 
.IR suffix .

Definitions of the symbols above are as follows:
.TP 8
.I range
N | [start]-[end] | last:N
.TP 8
.I pattern
\&'key=val' | 'key==val' | 'key!=val' | 'key!==val'
| '!<pattern>' | '(<pattern>)'
| '<pattern>&<pattern>' | '<pattern>|<pattern>'
.PP
If built with iconv,
.B mewl
decodes encoded-words of RFC 2047 in a field body into UTF-8 before
comparing it with
.IR val ,
so
.I val
should be given in UTF-8.
.PP
If built with utf8proc,
the case-sensitive operators (== and !==) compare a field body with
.I val
after canonical composition (NFC), so that precomposed and decomposed
spellings of the same text agree while everything else is distinct.
The case-insensitive operators (= and !=) compare them
by Unicode full case folding and canonical composition (NFC), so that
"Stra\(sse" matches "STRASSE" and precomposed and decomposed spellings
agree.
If built with UTF8PROC_CHAR_FOLD
(configure --enable-utf8proc-char-fold; see INSTALL.md),
they also ignore compatibility differences such as width and default
ignorable characters such as variation selectors (NFKC_Casefold), so
that fullwidth and halfwidth forms match their ordinary ones.
Without utf8proc, or when either side is not valid UTF-8, they are
compared byte by byte; = and != then ignore the case of ASCII letters
only.
The key "head" (the whole header) and the body are compared as they
are, neither decoded nor normalized.

.\"
.SH BUGS
If a field is long, only the beginning three lines are extracted 
by default.
.\"
